Do you ever use wizard mode to try out this kind of thing?
You don't even have to shut down your current game. Just
start nethack with:

C:\(location of hack drive)\nethack.exe -u wizard -D

You can even start with an assortment of items for your
experiment if you create a text file: wizkit.txt and list
the things you want, one per line just like you were wishing
for them. Then use ^w to wish for anything you think of
later. You can get a list of the special commands by using
the ? command.

In this case, once you have a character outfitted much like
your own, use one of the special commands to conjure up
whatever method you plan to use to reduce your level and try
it out. A couple of the harder character variables to
duplicate are luck and alignment. You can wish for gems and
create a unicorn to fix the luck but I expect you'll just
have to create a bunch of monsters and kill them to get
alignment adjusted.
